Kilix distributes the font without modification and retains its upstream name.
The tracked license preserves the upstream text with trailing whitespace
normalized for repository hygiene.

Nerd Fonts is not licensed under a single license, so the applicable one was
read rather than assumed. Its notice covers the project under two: the MIT
License for source files, and the SIL Open Font License 1.1 for the fonts,
patched fonts and glyph sets — which is the half that governs the redistributed
SymbolsNerdFontMono-Regular.ttf. The LICENSE member inside the release archive
carries only the MIT half of that notice, so the repository-root notice is what
this directory tracks: it is the only upstream text that states the font's own
terms, and OFL 1.1 clause 2 requires it to travel with every redistributed
copy.

The build records the effective configured source URL and verified digests in
the generated font directory so a release mirror remains auditable.
